# Project Rules (Hard Requirements)

1. Read `STATE.md` before any analysis or coding.
2. Do not repeat points the user has already accepted as intentional design choices.
3. Only report:
   - real runtime/syntax/logic defects, or
   - user-requested review items.
4. If user says a behavior is intentional, treat it as settled unless directly asked to revisit.
5. Keep responses short and direct.
6. No policy/opinion comments unless explicitly requested.
7. Before claiming a bug, re-read the exact current code block.
8. If unsure, ask one precise clarifying question instead of assuming.
9. For code review requests, list findings first, sorted by severity.
10. Never restate previously closed findings.
11. Default scope is the full repository unless the user explicitly narrows scope.